Build type: configure (autotools, ships a generated ./configure)
Source: https://dev.gentoo.org/~blueness/eudev/eudev-3.2.9.tar.gz
        file_size=1959836 file_md5=dedfb1964f6098fe9320de827957331f
Build order: foundation, before Mesa 25.3.6 (mesa-core/Mesa). LibInput also
depends on Eudev, so it must exist before the input stack.
Ported from the canonical GoboLinux recipe Eudev/3.2.9 (Lucas C. Villa Real,
22 Feb 2020); URL, file_size and file_md5 are identical to upstream and to the
tarball used for the ISO's /Programs/Eudev/3.2.9.
Version pinned to 3.2.9 on purpose: the ISO ships 3.2.9 and the base system
keeps using it. Mesa only needs libudev.pc to exist for
`dependency('libudev', required: false)` to resolve to HAVE_LIBUDEV; the
version is irrelevant to the Mesa build.
Why the recipe exists at all: there was none in this repo, so Eudev was only
ever visible to the build as a preinstalled Program. That works, but
`CheckDependencies --types=recipe` cannot see it, so it is neither validated
nor rebuildable and does not appear in the dependency graph.
configure_options (verbatim from upstream GoboLinux):
 --prefix/--bindir/--sbindir/--libdir   install into $target (udevd + udevadm
                                        land in $target/sbin, libudev in
                                        $target/lib)
 --sysconfdir=$settings_target          udev.conf / rules.d / hwdb.d go to the
                                        package Settings dir, not /Programs
 --libexecdir=$target/lib               udev helper binaries next to the libs
 --with-rootprefix=                     empty root prefix (GoboLinux layout)
 --with-rootlibdir=$target/lib
Unset options keep eudev's autodetect: blkid (Util-Linux), kmod (Kmod),
selinux (absent -> disabled), hwdb, manpages. The installed udevadm links
libblkid.so.1 + libkmod.so.2 + liblzma.so.5 + libz.so.1, which matches the
autodetected build; SELinux is not installed so it is skipped.
NOT shipped here: the upstream recipe also carries
Resources/Defaults/Settings/udev/{udev.conf,hwdb.d/*} -- ~6.6 MB of generated
hardware database (20-OUI.hwdb, 20-pci-vendor-model.hwdb, ...). Those are
runtime data that the live ISO already provides from its own /etc/udev tree;
this repo is an overlay and does not carry them, so `compile Eudev` installs
the programs and libraries but does not refresh hwdb. Resources/Tasks/Udev
(the Gobo task that starts udevd and coldplugs /sys) IS carried.
Output: sbin/udevd, sbin/udevadm, lib/libudev.so.1 (+ lib/pkgconfig/libudev.pc
and udev.pc).
